      "revision": "Identity Studio and Group Scene retain Smartphone Snapshot Photo Reality v13 at 0.25 and their reversible rank-256 BF16 Turbo routes. Upgrade remains the approved d58732a whole-frame Base 9B path with no Turbo, source-latent initialization, generation mask, or second model pass. Its default-on deterministic_face_and_hair_local_v4 postprocess adds the restrained closed-mouth, warmth, fatigue/line, eye, stubble, and cheek/jaw treatment, reduces isolated cheek/nose dark dots with sparse local-median replacement, reduces broad artificial hair grooves, and slightly lifts existing brighter hair material only inside an eroded semantic ParseNet mask. It protects the first eight hair-boundary pixels and changes zero pixels outside the face/hair/iris masks; final six-reference gaze-locked identity is 0.7476. Phone-off now applies a deterministic post-decode natural-lens background finish using the hash-locked local U2Net human matte, subject-excluding normalized Gaussian blur, and exact protected-subject copy-back; the accepted prototype changed 64.4717% of background pixels with 0 / 255 protected-subject error. Smartphone v13 remains the separate phone-on path at 0.25, preserves its accepted deep-focus rendering, and skips the background finish entirely. Earlier prompt-only, Turbo, generative masked, broad-inpaint, and auto-promoted Smartphone Upgrade routes remain rejected. Group Scene defaults Turbo off and keeps the concise identity-first prompt recovered from the approved PNG, with appearance enhancement disabled; its reloaded 50-step result scored 0.5958 against six genuine held-outs with no leakage failure.",
